Question:
Write a JavaScript program to print only the vowels from a string.
 Example:
 Input: "hellow world"
 Output: e, o, o

Coding Solution
const vowels=new Set(['a','e','i','o','u']);
console.log(vowels)

const str="hellow world"
const result=[];
for (const a of str.toLowerCase()){
    console.log(a);
    if(vowels.has(a)){
        result.push(a);
    }
}
console.log(result.join(","));

